### Attempt 1
Rule:
The grid consists of blocks of color 8 (and sometimes 6) separated by rows/columns of zeros. The transformation changes some of the 8s to 4s based on adjacency to zeros within the same block. Specifically, for each contiguous region of 8s (a block), if the block is adjacent to a zero cell that is inside the block's bounding box but not part of the block (i.e., a hole inside the block), then the cells of the block that are adjacent to that zero are changed to 4. More simply: within each rectangular block of 8s, any 8 that is orthogonally adjacent to a zero inside the block's bounding box becomes 4. The zeros that are part of the separating lines (full rows/columns of zeros) are ignored. The 6 blocks remain unchanged.

